## ✅ Custom domain setup added

I created the GitHub Pages custom domain file at `CNAME` with:

the-fashion-hub.com

This is the file GitHub Pages uses when you want the site to load from the custom domain instead of the GitHub Pages URL.

### Final result
Your site is now configured for:
- https://the-fashion-hub.com

### Important
To make it live, you also need to:
1. Set the domain in your GitHub Pages settings
2. Point your DNS to GitHub Pages
3. Wait for DNS propagation

